  "Question": "Elisa swims laps in the pool. When she first started, she completed \\(10\\) laps in \\(25\\) minutes. Now, she can finish \\(12\\) laps in \\(24\\) minutes. By how many minutes has she improved her lap time?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{4}\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(2\\)",
    "E": "\\(3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Compare the time for one lap in each case by dividing the total time by the number of laps. Her original lap time was\n\\[\n25\\div10=2.5\\text{ minutes},\n\\]\nand her current lap time is\n\\[\n24\\div12=2\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nHer improvement is the decrease in time per lap:\n\\[\n2.5-2=0.5=\\frac12\\text{ minute}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac12}\\), choice A.",
